    Remove HA/Overseer (#4503)
    
    ## Summary
    
    Strip the residual HA/Overseer infrastructure left after PR #3898.
    
    - Delete `nvflare/ha/` (DummyOverseerAgent) and
    `nvflare/apis/overseer_spec.py` (SP, OverseerAgent).
    - Drop the `overseer_agent` parameter and lifecycle hooks
    (`start_overseer_agent`, `overseer_callback`, `set_primary_sp`,
    `_init_agent`, `_check_server_state`, `_turn_to_hot`/`_turn_to_cold`,
    `_switch_ssid`) from `FedServer`/`FedClient`/`SimulatorServer` and their
    deployers. The client now connects via a single
    `connect_to_server(target, scheme)` call sourced directly from the
    configured endpoint.
    - Collapse `server_state.py` to `ServerState` + `HotState`; remove
    `ColdState`, `Cold2HotState`, `Hot2ColdState`, `ShutdownState` and their
    fobs registrations.
    - Drop `--ha_mode`, `JobProcessArgs.HA_MODE`,
    `FLContextKey.SP_END_POINT`, the `sp_end_point`/overseer regex patterns,
    `validate_sp_string`, `OverseerRole`, `PropKey.OVERSEER_END_POINT`,
    `ProvFileName.{DEPLOYMENT,SERVICE}_OVERSEER_YAML`,
    `TemplateSectionKey.HELM_CHART_*_OVERSEER`, `FLARE_OVERSEER`, the
    dashboard `/api/v1/overseer/blob` endpoint,
    `DockerBuilder._build_overseer`, and the
    `__overseer__`/`helm_chart_*_overseer` template sections.
    - Remove the `overseer_agent` block from fed_server / fed_client
    templates and add a plain `target` field; drop `ha_mode` from
    `start_svr_sh`.
    - Strip the `overseer_agent` block from 21 example/test `project.yml`
    files; update tests to assert `servers[0].service.target` instead of
    `overseer_agent.args.sp_end_point`.
    - Make `persist_components` a no-op (HA-only path); the xgboost
    executor's overseer-based fallback is removed.
    
    ## Backward compatibility
    
    - An `overseer_agent` block in old `fed_server.json` / `fed_client.json`
    now logs a warning (`"obsolete and will be ignored"`) and is skipped
    instead of being instantiated.
    - An `overseer_agent` kwarg on `StaticFileBuilder` logs a warning and is
    ignored (unblocks old `project.yml` builders).
    - An `overseer` participant in old `project.yml` prints a warning and is
    dropped (previously raised `ValueError`).
    
    `ssid` is intentionally retained; it is now the server-session
    identifier for cell-message authentication, no longer HA-only.
    
